==English==

===Etymology===
Hindi from Sanskrit [[नमस्कार]] ''namaskāra'', from ''namas'': "to bow", "[[obeisance]]" and ''kāra'': "action".

===Interjection===
'''namaskar''' 
#respectful greetings

===Noun===
'''namaskar''' (countable)
# ''(Indian English)'' The use of the [[greet]]ing in which you put your hands together and then [[bow]] slightly.

